        257.5379333496094,
        525.4273071289062,
        266.6038818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thus, if x ∈Supp(K), the rule selects the assignment whose",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        275.48101806640625,
        558.031005859375,
        285.1048889160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "normalized distance is minimal; otherwise, it selects the",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        288.1533203125,
        558.0009155273438,
        297.05987548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "default control u0. In the present analysis, we take u0 to be",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        299.94891357421875,
        557.998046875,
        310.50885009765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the zero input, so that when the state lies outside Supp(K),",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        311.3459777832031,
        558.0206909179688,
        320.9698486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the system follows the zero-input dynamics until it re-enters",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        324.0182800292969,
        558.0010375976562,
        332.9248352050781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the support of the assignment set. Building on this rule, we",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        335.9732666015625,
        558.0009765625,
        344.87982177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "now formalize the induced nonparametric policy.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        347.92926025390625,
        513.57763671875,
        356.8358154296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Definition 7 (Nonparametric Chain Policy). Given an as-",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        369.73870849609375,
        558.0010986328125,
        378.76483154296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "signment set K and a default control u0, the nonparametric",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        381.095947265625,
        557.9981079101562,
        391.4158020019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "chain policy (NCP) is the map",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000732421875,
        393.8589172363281,
        438.9578552246094,
        402.4466857910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "πK : X →A",
      "bbox": [
        409.3080749511719,
        411.7309265136719,
        461.8990173339844,
        422.630615234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "defined by πK(x) = uιK(x).",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000732421875,
        430.9688415527344,
        425.75970458984375,
        441.6502685546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Remark 2 (Execution of the Nonparametric Chain Policy).",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001037597656,
        452.93865966796875,
        558.0010986328125,
        461.96478271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Given an initial state x0 = x, the policy πK induces",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001037597656,
        464.85382080078125,
        558.0009155273438,
        475.194580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "an infinite-horizon control signal by concatenation. For",
      "bbox": [
        313.20013427734375,
        477.057861328125,
        558.0010375976562,
        485.6456298828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "each n ≥0, define recursively un := πK(xn), Tn :=",
      "bbox": [
        313.20013427734375,
        488.20587158203125,
        558.004638671875,
        499.1055603027344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "τ(un), xn+1 := ϕ(Tn, xn, un), where τ(un) denotes the",
      "bbox": [
        313.20013427734375,
        500.71978759765625,
        558.0026245117188,
        511.060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "duration of the selected control snippet un. Let s0 := 0",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        512.6747436523438,
        558.0035400390625,
        523.0155029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and sn+1 := sn + Tn. Then the induced control signal",
      "bbox": [
        313.2002258300781,
        524.6297607421875,
        558.0025024414062,
        534.9705200195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uK,x : (0, ∞) →U is defined by",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        536.02685546875,
        446.47314453125,
        546.926513671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uK,x(t) := un(t −sn),",
      "bbox": [
        347.8251953125,
        554.7069091796875,
        441.90826416015625,
        565.0256958007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t ∈[sn, sn+1).",
      "bbox": [
        463.4972229003906,
        554.7069091796875,
        523.3782348632812,
        565.0256958007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "III. REACHABILITY IN HAMILTONIAN SYSTEMS",
      "bbox": [
        333.26519775390625,
        578.1011962890625,
        537.939453125,
        587.0077514648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We are now ready to present the main results of this",
      "bbox": [
        323.1632080078125,
        617.1751708984375,
        558.0015869140625,
        626.0817260742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "paper. We establish target reachability by combining two",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        629.1301879882812,
        558.0012817382812,
        638.0367431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ingredients: local control actions that reduce an energy-",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        641.086181640625,
        558.001220703125,
        649.9927368164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "based distance to the target, and recurrence of the zero-",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        653.0411376953125,
        558.0012817382812,
        661.9476928710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "input Hamiltonian flow, which returns trajectories to regions",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        664.9961547851562,
        558.0011596679688,
        673.9027099609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where those actions can be reused. Repeating this interplay",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        676.951171875,
        558.0011596679688,
        685.8577270507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "allows the trajectory to reach the target energy band and,",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        688.9061889648438,
        558.0010986328125,
        697.812744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ultimately, the target set. This separation between controlled",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        700.8621826171875,
        558.0012817382812,
        709.7687377929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "energy reduction and passive recurrence underlies all results",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        712.8171997070312,
        558.0010375976562,
        721.7237548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in this section.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2001953125,
        724.7721557617188,
        373.0355224609375,
        733.6787109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
